# Excluded from the sandbox build context — and, more importantly, from the CONTENT HASH that names
# the E2B template / Daytona snapshot (remote-box's image_name() honors this file, rooted here at
# examples/, because examples/ is the SandboxConfig's local_project_root).
#
# Without this, editing any file anywhere under examples/ — including a README, or a stray
# __pycache__ — changes the image name, so the prebuilt image "disappears" and the next run fails
# `require_prebuilt` (E2B: "template 'sandboxed-coding-agent-<hash>' not found") until you rebuild.
# Prose has no business invalidating an image, so it is excluded here.
#
# Only exclude things the Dockerfiles never COPY. Both sandbox Dockerfiles copy an explicit list of
# .py files plus one .sh, so none of these patterns can remove something the image needs.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.md
